            "correct_answer": "C",
            "solution_explanation": "C is correct. Standards of conduct are applied to specific communities or societal \ngroups and identify specific behaviors required of community members. These \nstandards of conduct serve as benchmarks for the minimally acceptable behav­\nior of community members. Codes of ethics serve as a general guide for how \ncommunity members should act; they communicate the organization's values \nand overall expectations regarding member behavior, but they do not identify \nspecific behaviors required of community members. Laws and regulations are \nrules of conduct defined by governments and related entities about obligatory \nand forbidden conduct broadly applicable for individuals and entities under their \njurisdiction."
