            "options": {
              "A": "Neither statement violated the Code and Standards.",
              "B": "Only statement I violated the Code and Standards.",
              "C": "Only statement II violated the Code and Standards."
            },
            "correct_answer": null,
            "solution_explanation": "The correct answer is C. This question involves Standard I(C) Misrepresentation. \nStatement I is a factual statement that discloses to clients and prospects accurate \ninformation about the terms of the investment instrument. Statement II, which \nguarantees a specific rate of return for a mutual fund, is an opinion stated as \na fact and, therefore, violates Standard I(C). If statement II were rephrased to \ninclude a qualifying statement, such as \"in my opinion, investors may earn . . . , \" \nit would not be in violation of the Standards. \nSee Standard I(C): Misrepresentation"
