            "solution_explanation": "Choice C is correct. The expected return combines the price increase from \nGBP54 to GBP60, the dividends paid, and the return generated from the return \non reinvested dividends as follows:\n\tPrice return = 11.11% [= (60 - 54) ÷ 54]\n\tDividend return incorporating reinvestment = 3.76% (= 2.03 ÷ 54)\n\tCompounded value of dividends = GBP2.03 \n\t[= 0.50(1.01)3 + 0.50(1.01)2 + 0.50(1.01)1 + 0.50]\n\tTotal return = 14.87% (= 11.11% + 3.76%), which rounds to 14.9%.\nChoice A is incorrect because 11.11% reflects only the price change.\nChoice B is incorrect because 14.8% reflects only the dividends paid without \nincorporating the return earned on dividend reinvestment."
