            "solution_explanation": "Choice C is correct. A stock split lowers the per share price by increasing the \nnumber of shares outstanding to keep the price per share at a level low enough to \nattract interest from retail investors.\nChoice A is incorrect because institutional investors are less likely to respond to \nthe price per share changes created by stock splits.\nChoice B is incorrect because this statement better describes a reverse stock split \nas an attempt to improve the stock price optics by increasing the price per share."
