            "solution_explanation": "Choice C is correct. The two-year holding period return on Bryce Limited shares \nis closest to 141%. The following table shows the share price and dividend details \nover the two-year holding period:\n\nSolutions\n103\nBryce Limited Share Price and Dividend Details\nMeasure / Time\nt = −2\nt = −1\nt = 0\nPrice\n76\n96\n82\nDividend\n-\n5\n5\nSplit factor\n-\n2\n-\nSplit-adjusted price\n38\n48\n-\nSplit-adjusted dividend\n-\n2.50\n-\nComputing the two-period return from the split-adjusted prices and dividends \nyields the following:\n\tr  =  140.87%  =   \n[(82 + 5) × (1 +  2.50 \n_ \n48 ) − 38] \n \n \n_____________________ \n \n38   .\nChoice A is incorrect because 20.4% is only obtained if the computation fails to \naccount for the split from a year earlier.\nChoice B is incorrect because 127% is obtained if the computation fails to ac­\ncount for the dividend just received."
