            "correct_answer": "B",
            "solution_explanation": "B is correct. Choice B is correct because Lough's net debt to assets is only 4.2%. \nNet debt is equal to EV minus equity market capitalization, so Lough's net debt is \n1,000 (= 26,000 − 25,000). Dividing this by Lough's book value of assets of 24,000 \ngives a result of 4.2% (= 1,000 ÷ 24,000).\nChoice A is incorrect because Rivercreek's net debt to assets is 22.2%. Its net debt \nis 10,000 (= 200,000 − 190,000), and its book value of assets is 45,000.\n\nLearning Module 5\t\nIntroduction to Equity Valuation\n144\nChoice C is incorrect because Arkanoid's net debt to assets is 20%. Its net debt is \n5,000 (= 105,000 − 100,000), and its book value of assets is 25,000."
