            "correct_answer": "B",
            "solution_explanation": "B is correct because StevCo's justified value-to-book multiple assuming constant \ngrowth is approximately 1.11, as shown below.\n\tStevCo return on capital  =   \nEBIT t+1 × (1 − t) \n \n_______________ \n \nBook value of capital\n   =   (300 − 150) × (1 − 0.30) \n \n_________________ \n \n400 + 900   \n\t=  8.077%.\nIn the previous equation, StevCo's EBIT is calculated by subtracting depreciation \nof EUR150 million from its EBITDA of EUR300 million. Then, in the equation \nbelow, StevCo's reinvestment rate is computed by subtracting depreciation from \ncapital expenditures of EUR190 million. The resulting EUR40 million is divided \nby StevCo's after-tax EBIT as shown in the numerator of the return on capital \ncalculation.\n\tJustified value to book  =   \nReturn on capital  ×  (1 - Reinvestment rate) \n \n \n \n________________________________ \n \nWACC − g    \n\tStevCo justified value to book  =   \n0.08077  × (1 −  190 − 150 \n_ \n105 ) \n \n___________________ \n \n0.075 − 0.03    =  1.11.\nA is incorrect because this result occurs if the reinvestment rate is incorrectly \ncalculated by omitting depreciation in the numerator and using after-tax EBIT­\nDA in the denominator of the reinvestment rate equation.\nC is incorrect because this result occurs if after-tax EBITDA is incorrectly used \nto calculate return on capital."
