            "correct_answer": "A",
            "solution_explanation": "A is correct. Both inventory-sales and unit labor costs are lagging indicators that \ndecline somewhat after a peak. Real personal income is a coincident indicator \nthat, by its decline, shows a slowdown in business activity."
