              "C": "accept the alternative hypothesis that the money supply growth changed.\nThe following information relates to questions \n8-11\nAhmed Khaled, CFA, is preparing a research report on Shaams Renewable Ener­\ngy Corp., one of the largest renewable energy companies in the Middle East, fo­\ncused on solar and wind power. Khaled aims to assess the sensitivity of Shaams's \nstock returns to various economic factors. A client recently asked whether \nShaams's stock tends to rise after increases in non-renewable energy prices, such \nas oil and natural gas. While Khaled believes the relationship is negative, he is \nunsure of its strength.\nHe directs his assistant, Fatima Al-Mansoori, to analyze the relationships \nbetween:"
