            "correct_answer": null,
            "solution_explanation": "The correct response is C. The sample variance is calculated by dividing the total \nsum of squares (SST), 95.2, by the degrees of freedom (n − 1), where n = 5. Thus, \nthe sample variance is:\n\t SST \n_ \nn − 1\n   =   95.2 \n_ \n5 − 1\n   =  23.80.\nAlternative A is incorrect: 1.55 is the standard error of the estimate (SEE). The \nstandard error of the estimate is the square root of the mean square error (MSE), \nwhich is 2.4:\n\tSEE  =  √ _ \n2.4   ≈  1.55.\nAlternative B is incorrect: It results from incorrectly dividing the total sum of \nsquares by n = 5 and not n − 1.\n\nLearning Module 10\t\nApplications of Simple Linear Regression in Finance\n572"
